.TH "CRASHREPORT" "3JS" "April 21, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CrashReport \- CrashReport
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]CrashReport\f[R] dictionary of the Reporting API represents a
crash report.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] It is not possible to retrieve crash reports using a
\f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] \(em the reports are only generated when
the browser crashes, at which point the observer code isn\(cqt available
to run.
.RE
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]age\f[R]
The age of the report in milliseconds.
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
The string \f[CR]\(dqcrash\(dq\f[R] indicating that this is a crash
report.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R]
A string representing the URL of the document that generated the report.
.TP
\f[B]user_agent\f[R]
The user agent string of the browser that generated the report.
.TP
\f[B]body\f[R]
The body of the report.
This is an object with the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]crash_report_api\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object containing the key\-value pairs set via the
\f[CR]CrashReportContext.set()\f[R] method, if any.
.TP
\f[B]is_top_level\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether the crashed document was a top\-level
document (\f[CR]true\f[R]) or an embedded document (\f[CR]false\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]reason\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string indicating the specific reason why the crash occurred, if
known.
Possible values are:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]oom\f[R]
The page ran out of memory.
.TP
\f[B]unresponsive\f[R]
The page was killed due to being unresponsive.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]stack\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string representing the JavaScript call stack at the time of the
crash.
This is included if the \f[CR]reason\f[R] is \f[CR]unresponsive\f[R], if
the \f[CR]Document\-Policy\f[R] value for
\f[CR]include\-js\-call\-stacks\-in\-crash\-reports\f[R] in the document
that crashed is \f[CR]true\f[R], and if the call stack was able to be
recovered from the crashed document.
.TP
\f[B]visibility_state\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
An enumerated value indicating whether the document is visible.
This mirrors the value of the \f[CR]Document.visibilityState\f[R]
property.
Possible values are:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]visible\f[R]
The document content is at least partially visible.
.TP
\f[B]hidden\f[R]
The document content is completely hidden.
.RE
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Crash reports containing arbitrary information can be sent to a server
endpoint using the Reporting API .
This is useful because we can store detailed diagnostic information
throughout the lifetime of an application and use the reports to debug
crashes more effectively.
.PP
The diagnostic information is stored in a special key\-value store that
can be manipulated using the document\(cqs \f[CR]CrashReportContext\f[R]
object.
This is accessed via the \f[CR]Window.crashReport\f[R] property.
.PP
When the browser crashes, the information stored in the key\-value store
is added to a \f[CR]CrashReport\f[R] and sent to a reporting server.
The reporting server endpoint and its mapping to a particular URL are
set using the \f[CR]Reporting\-Endpoints\f[R] header.
.IP \(bu 2
If a \f[CR]crash\-reporting\f[R] server endpoint is defined, crash
reports are delivered there.
For example:
.RS 2
.IP
.EX
Reporting\-Endpoints: crash\-reporting=\(dqhttps://example.com/reports\(dq
.EE
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
If a \f[CR]crash\-reporting\f[R] endpoint is not defined, but a
\f[CR]default\f[R] reporting server endpoint is defined, crash reports
are delivered there.
For example:
.RS 2
.IP
.EX
Reporting\-Endpoints: default=\(dqhttps://example.com/reports\(dq
.EE
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
If neither endpoint is defined, crash reports are not delivered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Sending a report to a reporting endpoint
Configuring a web page to send a crash report requires that you define a
reporting server endpoint using the \f[CR]Reporting\-Endpoints\f[R]
header, for example \f[CR]https://example.com/reports\f[R], as described
earlier.
.PP
A typical report structure is as follows:
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqage\(dq: 27,
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqcrash\(dq,
  \(dqurl\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
  \(dquser_agent\(dq: \(dqMozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0\(dq,
  \(dqbody\(dq: {
    \(dqsourceFile\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
    \(dqreason\(dq: \(dqunresponsive\(dq,
    \(dqstack\(dq: \(dqSomeError: ... at ...\(dq,
    \(dqis_top_level\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R],
    \(dqvisibility_state\(dq: \(dqvisible\(dq,
    \(dqcrash_report_api\(dq: {
      \(dqcrash_data_1\(dq: \(dq0001\(dq,
      \(dqcrash_data_2\(dq: \(dq0002\(dq
    }
  }
}
.EE
.PP
The report will be sent as a JSON object in a \f[CR]POST\f[R] request to
the endpoint whenever the browser crashes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CrashReportContext\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Reporting\-Endpoints\f[R]
